{"additions":484,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPart of #148, closes #153 — the last sub-issue.\n\n- **`domain/filter.rs`** parses `ProjectV2View.filter` and evaluates it against the items already fetched — no extra API call — before grouping and sorting, in the table, board (lanes) and roadmap alike.\n- **Supported**: free-text title words, `field:value` with `,` lists and quoted values (`status:\"In Progress\"`), `-` negation, `is:issue|pr|draft`, `no:<field>` / `has:<field>`, `assignee:` (`@me` resolves to the signed-in login, fetched once per session with `gh api user` — REST, zero GraphQL points), `label:`, `milestone:`, `repo:` (full `owner/repo` or the short name), and `<any field>:value` on custom fields.\n- **Unsupported, reported not applied**: ranges / comparisons (`>`, `<`, `..`), wildcards, `is:open|closed|merged` (item-list carries no state), `updated:` / `created:` / `reviewer:` … — the status bar shows `⚠ filter: unsupported \"…\"`; an `@me` before the login is known never matches until it arrives.\n- Status bar counts what the filter hid: `8 items in 3 columns (3 filtered out)`; `item_count` / `filtered_out` on the pane.\n\n## Docs\n\nGuide (en/ja) Projects chapter: a filter paragraph in the saved-views section.\n\n## Demo\n\nThe demo project's views carry no filter, so the existing GIF is unchanged. To show it, a filter can be put on the `By status` view with `updateProjectV2View` (e.g. `-status:Done`) and the tape re-recorded — offered separately.\n\n## Tests\n\nTokenizer (quoted values), field / list / negation semantics, `is:` / `no:` / `has:` / `label:` / `assignee:@me` / `repo:` / free text, unsupported-token reporting, plus a pane test covering every layout, the status-bar notice, view switching and late `@me` resolution. 378 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Qxrr9mRdnw87JU1D28bRQo\n","changedFiles":8,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:37Z","deletions":3,"headRefName":"feat/projects-view-filter","labels":[],"number":166,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMcIVqQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new filter parser uses `raw.starts_with(['>', '<'])`, which is not a valid `str::starts_with` pattern on stable Rust and will fail to compile.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR completes the Projects saved-view feature by parsing each `ProjectV2View.filter` expression and evaluating it locally against already-fetched items (no extra API calls), applying the result consistently across Table / Board / Roadmap layouts and reflecting hidden/unsupported filter effects in the status bar.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added a local filter parser/matcher (`src/projects/domain/filter.rs`) supporting a practical subset of GitHub Projects filter syntax, with unsupported tokens reported but ignored.\n- Integrated filtering into Projects board pane sorting/grouping/lane building, plus status bar counts and unsupported-token notices.\n- Added background fetching of the signed-in viewer login (`gh api user`) to support `assignee:@me` filters, with tests and docs updates.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Fetches viewer login once per Projects session and wires it into the board pane. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Applies parsed view filters across all layouts; reports filtered-out count and unsupported tokens; adds coverage tests. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/mod.rs | Exposes the new filter module. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/filter.rs | Implements tokenizer/parser and matcher for saved-view filter expressions with unsupported-token reporting. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Adds `viewer_login()` via `gh api user` for `assignee:@me`. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Shows filtered-out item count and unsupported-filter notices in Projects status bar. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Documents supported/unsupported filter behavior and status bar messages (EN). |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Documents supported/unsupported filter behavior and status bar messages (JA). |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 8/8 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:37:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"1396e110a338f19926823472af702c6b31c33180"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMcNmpQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:45:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"1396e110a338f19926823472af702c6b31c33180"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:48:26Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34102556357/job/101680085824","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:48:26Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:39:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320839/job/101676199558","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:35:20Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320921/job/101676199371","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:44Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:38:09Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320839/job/101676199533","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:41:06Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320839/job/101676199300","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:41:06Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320839/job/101678004347","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:41:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:48:26Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34102556357/job/101680112550","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:48:32Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T08:35:53Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34101320921/job/101676199614","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T08:34:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T0